    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 3 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Form the best three-card Brag hand. Do not have the worst hand when someone calls Stop the Bus; the lowest hand loses a life.',
      "Turn-flow example: Dealer deals three cards each and turns one card face up to start the discard pile; the rest form the stock. Player to dealer's left starts; play is clockwise. On your turn you may: (1) Draw the top card of the stock (face down), add it to your hand, then discard one of your four cards face up onto the discard pile; (2) Draw the top card of the discard pile, add it to your hand, then discard a different card from your hand face up; or (3) Call 'Stop the Bus' and keep your current three cards without drawing or discarding. When someone calls Stop the Bus, each other player has one more turn (they may pass without drawing). All then show hands; the player with the worst Brag hand loses one life (token). A player with no tokens left is eliminated. Play continues with new deals until one player remains.",
      'Scoring example: Form the best three-card Brag hand. The player with the worst hand when someone calls Stop the Bus loses a life; last player remaining wins. Form the best three-card Brag hand. Do not have the worst hand when Stop the Bus is called; last player with tokens wins..',
